# Cursor Rules for cursor-cloud-agent-tests

## Project Overview
This is a test repository for Cursor cloud agent functionality. It is designed to validate and test the integration between Cursor IDE and cloud-based AI agents.

## General Guidelines
- Keep code simple and well-documented
- Follow best practices for the specific language/framework being tested
- Include clear comments explaining test scenarios
- Maintain consistency across test files

## Testing Standards
- Write clear and descriptive test names
- Include both positive and negative test cases
- Document expected behaviors
- Keep tests isolated and independent

## Code Style
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Keep functions small and focused
- Add comments for complex logic
- Follow language-specific conventions

## AI Assistant Behavior
- Provide context-aware suggestions
- Help maintain code quality and consistency
- Suggest improvements and optimizations
- Assist with debugging and troubleshooting
